s or independents toward Rogers, or a polling miss in either direction, could move this into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gary Peters (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's open Senate seat is one of the closest races of the cycle, with Democrat Abdul El-Sayed facing Republican Mike Rogers to succeed retiring Senator Gary Peters. Recent polls show El-Sayed narrowly ahead, with margins mostly between one and five points, and averages cluster around a two-to-three-point Democratic edge. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean or Tilt Democratic, though several rate it a tossup, and prediction markets give El-Sayed roughly a 69-70% chance of winning.\n\nThe race has been expensive and combative, with more than $21 million in outside spending opposing El-Sayed and heated final debates centered on trust and loyalty questions. Republicans are working to make inroads with Black voters, while Sanders' $1 million donation highlights continued progressive energy behind El-Sayed. The evidence points to a narrow but real Democratic advantage heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7427, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-1